    "pd_decision_conflict": "I keep going back and forth, and it will not settle.",
    "sys_consequence_reasoning": "even though it means five years alone while they walk free"
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I am stuck between those two versions of myself and neither one feels bearable."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "makes my chest tight with doubt."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I keep circling both options and neither one lets me rest.",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "carry the whole weight myself, and that thought alone makes it hard to breathe"
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I cannot get my mind to stop turning it over.",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "terrified that holding onto it makes me naive."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I genuinely do not know which discomfort I can live with."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "But I am not at peace with it",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "the fear of carrying it alone gnaws at me constantly."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "There is no comfortable place to land in this."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I feel pulled in two directions at once, and neither pull loosens.",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "fear of what that silence costs me personally does not go away."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "My mind will not settle on either path",
    "pd_personal_consequence_anxiety": "wants to protect myself from being naive twice over."
  }
]
